      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11378927::web::018::electrochemical_behavior_of_cocrfenimocu"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The passive oxide film is self-healing and formed in equilibrium with the NaCl electrolyte.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continuity of the passive oxide film protects the underlying alloy from corrosion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12839976::web::023::3_3_passive_film_characteristics"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled sliding wear mechanically disrupts and removes the passive oxide film.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Passive-film disruption gives chloride ions increased access to freshly exposed metal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased chloride access to fresh metal accelerates localized corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Passive-film disruption and the resulting localized corrosion govern the overall tribo-corrosion degradation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combined sliding and corrosion produce a higher overall degradation rate than static immersion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11378927::web::018::electrochemical_behavior_of_cocrfenimocu"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sliding in NaCl will increase localized corrosion at the wear track and reduce its electrochemical impedance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11378927::web::018::electrochemical_behavior_of_cocrfenimocu"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Visible corrosion pits will develop at the wear track.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The combined sliding-corrosion specimen will have a larger wear volume than the static-immersion baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coupled degradation will be significantly greater than the sum of isolated wear and isolated corrosion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
